## Best Practices for Smooth Performance

### Performance (MANDATORY)
- ✅ **RequestAnimationFrame** for all animations and drag/resize
- ✅ **Dynamic imports** for code splitting (reduce initial bundle)
- ✅ **Debounce** resize handlers (150ms)
- ✅ **React.memo** for pure components
- ✅ **useMemo** for expensive computations
- ✅ **useCallback** for event handlers in dependencies
- ✅ **Refs** for frequently updated values during animations
- ✅ **Batched updates** - collect updates, apply in single operation
- ✅ **CSS transitions** instead of JS animations when possible
- ✅ **Transform/opacity** for animations (GPU-accelerated)
- ✅ **will-change** for known animations
- ✅ **Passive event listeners** for touch/scroll events

### Code Quality
- ✅ ESLint configured (Next.js + TypeScript rules)
- ✅ Prettier configured (auto-format on save)
- ✅ No unused variables (prefix with `_` if intentionally unused)
- ✅ All dependencies in hooks listed
- ✅ Type safety enforced

### Image Optimization
- ✅ Use Next.js `Image` component (not `<img>`)
- ✅ Use `unoptimized` prop for external images (Unsplash)
- ✅ Proper width/height attributes
- ✅ Lazy loading for images below fold

### Error Handling
- ✅ Error boundaries for Desktop & Mobile modes
- ✅ Graceful fallbacks for API failures (battery, network)
- ✅ Try-catch for async operations

## Common Patterns

### Adding New App
1. Add app metadata to `stores/apps.ts` (defaultApps array)
2. Create component in `components/Apps/`
3. Add component mapping in `utils/appComponents.tsx`
4. Export component type in `types/index.ts` (AppComponentName)

### Window Operations (Performance Critical)
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT Pattern for Window Operations
// 1. Use refs during drag/resize
const stateRef = useRef({ /* state */ });

// 2. Batch updates with RAF
const rafRef = useRef<number | null>(null);
const pendingUpdate = useRef({});

const handleMouseMove = useCallback((e: MouseEvent) => {
  // Update refs (no re-render)
  const updates = calculateUpdates(e);
  Object.assign(pendingUpdate.current, updates);
  
  // Schedule RAF
  if (!rafRef.current) {
    rafRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(() => {
      updateWindow(id, pendingUpdate.current);
      pendingUpdate.current = {};
      rafRef.current = null;
    });
  }
}, []);

// 3. Final update on mouseup
const handleMouseUp = useCallback(() => {
  if (rafRef.current) cancelAnimationFrame(rafRef.current);
  updateWindow(id, pendingUpdate.current);
}, []);
```

### Device Detection
```typescript
const deviceInfo = detectDevice();
// Returns: { platform, isMobile, isTablet, isDesktop, screenWidth, screenHeight, hasTouch }
```

